<p>UK recruitment agencies operate in a fast-moving, highly competitive market. The agencies that win are the ones that find the right candidates first, build stronger relationships, and spend less time on admin. AI is reshaping how the best agencies work, and the gap between AI-enabled agencies and the rest is widening quickly.</p>
<p>The problem with generic AI tools is that they don't understand recruitment. Off-the-shelf CV parsers miss sector-specific terminology. Chatbot screening tools ask irrelevant questions that frustrate candidates. Generic matching algorithms keyword-match without understanding what actually makes a candidate right for a role. They create more noise, not more placements.</p>
<p>Bespoke AI solutions are built around your agency's specialism and workflow. We train CV parsing and matching models on your sector's language, whether that's construction, healthcare, tech, or finance. We build screening logic that reflects your consultants' judgement, not a generic rubric. We create outreach automation that sounds like your agency, not a robot, and that responds intelligently to candidate replies.</p>
<p>Compliance is critical in recruitment AI. You are processing personal data of candidates, which is subject to UK GDPR. AI screening must be transparent, fair, and free from discriminatory bias. We build with explainability in mind, ensuring you can tell a candidate why they were or weren't shortlisted. We also ensure data retention and subject access requests are handled correctly when AI is part of the pipeline.</p>
<p>We worked with a UK technical recruitment agency placing 200+ contractors per year. Consultants were spending 40% of their time on CV sourcing and screening. Our AI-powered matching tool, integrated with Bullhorn, reduced sourcing time by 55% and increased the number of qualified shortlists per consultant per week from 3 to 7. The automated outreach module improved response rates from passive candidates by 32%, opening up a previously untapped talent pool. Interview summarisation reduced post-interview admin from 30 minutes to 5 minutes per candidate, and the placement prediction model helped consultants prioritise roles with the highest close probability, improving overall placement conversion from 22% to 31%.</p>

